          "text": "HESU 和素 (T. 存齋, 純德), 1652–1718, Manchu official and translator, was a member of the Wanyen clan and of the Bordered Yellow Banner. He was the second son of Asitan [q. v.] and was well versed in Manchu and Chinese.",
